WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.880
Mō tātou, a, mō ka uri a muri ake nei

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:17.670
In August we were pleased to officially open
Feldwick drive.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:23.779
We had a great turn out both from local residents,
and the vintage car enthusiasts.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:28.910
The Riverview Terraces continue to make good
progress, with the riverbank now looking a

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.560
lot tidier and the seating areas starting
to take shape.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.949
When we developed the Recovery Plan for these
areas, the community really clearly told us

00:00:40.949 --> 00:00:42.979
which facilities they wanted to have.

00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:47.030
The draft Reserves Master Plan is effectively
a blueprint which shows how all those ideas

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.769
fit together in this space.

00:00:49.769 --> 00:00:53.449
Developing the Reserves Masterplan is the
last key planning and design exercise before

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:54.579
we get into construction.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:00:59.579
It's look at where the activities and features
will go, where pathways go, where we'll have

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:03.260
some key planting, where the stormwater management
areas are.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.690
One key project is the construction of multipurpose
sport fields with changing rooms, toilets,

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:08.690
and parking.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:13.210
It’s also planned to build two dedicated
softball diamonds, these will help cater for

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.810
the huge growth in the sport and allow tournaments
to be hosted in our district.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:21.860
11 years ago we were two teams, we're very
close to 20.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:28.950
It gives them the ability to have some very
good facilities to play on rather than just

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:29.950
a bit of dirt.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.869
The planned dog park will have areas for both
small and large dogs.

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:38.560
We’re keeping many of the existing trees,
so it will look well established right from

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.560
the opening.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.560
This has consistently been one of the most
requested facilities for the Regeneration

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.560
Areas.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.020
I think there needs to be somewhere fenced
off close by for dogs and owners to be able

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.860
to let their dogs of the leash.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:54.920
I think rubbish bins is a big thing that a
dog park needs and somewhere for the dogs

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.560
to be able to have a drink.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.080
Careful thought and planning has gone into
making sure the reserves can be enjoyed by everyone.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.000
Throughout all the new reserves, we've tried
to maximise walking and cycling tracks.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.840
The tracks will link up to existing reserves
and to some of the key activities and features

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.520
we're proposing.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.760
You can find out more about the draft Master
Reserves plan on the council website.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.159
The first projects to get underway will be
the stormwater management areas, and work

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:23.530
will start on those in the next month.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:28.400
We’ll take a closer look at the progress
in those in our next update.

